Z||000001||fastonpumpgas||10-20-1999||05:20 PM||||I have seen them alot, but hte problem I ran into is that the lowered springs are just cut off stock springs that are new and painted red.  If you find any with the same amount of coils as stock but lowered, please post it ....||||reg||1
Z||000002||88 Fiero||10-20-1999||05:40 PM||||I don't think there are any available '88 lowered springs... Eibach discontinued it.. As far as the Fiero Store they are just Springs that are cut down. Suspension Techniques and Eibach still makes the springs for the '84 to '87 but not '88's.... I have an '88 formula with a modified body and my car's springs were cut... I will be purchasing a Coils Over instead that way I could play with the rate of the springs... I already got that info that I need... Plus I am going 9 inch wide in the rear....||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eddie||10-20-1999||05:55 PM||||I have a 1987 and I had the springs cut . The front hit hard .But I love the ones in the back for some reason the rear doesn,t try to push the front into the next lane when I hit in turns. the guy that cut my springs is going to put lowering springs on the front monday FREE LABOR $80.00 FOR THE SPRINGS.||||reg||4
